---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Sniffr Roadmap — 2026"
  description="The order we're shipping in, and roughly when. Every line below is real, partially built, and on the calendar through 2026 into early 2027."
>
  <article class="px-6 py-20 md:py-28">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <header>
        <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-widest text-[var(--color-accent)] font-semibold">
          Roadmap
        </p>
        <h1 class="font-display text-5xl md:text-7xl font-semibold tracking-tight mt-3 text-balance">
          Sniffr 2026
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-8 text-lg md:text-xl text-[var(--color-muted)] leading-relaxed">
          Sniffr is built by one founder using a custom AI agent infrastructure that
          ships features at the pace of a small team. Everything below is real, partially
          built, and on the calendar. We'll move dates as we learn, but not by years.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-lg md:text-xl text-[var(--color-muted)] leading-relaxed">
          The order matters. Sniffr grows on two sides &mdash; the businesses that do the
          work, and the record that belongs to the dog &mdash; and each phase below feeds
          the next.
        </p>
      </header>

      <!-- V1 -->
      <section class="mt-20">
        <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between flex-wrap gap-2">
          <h2 class="font-display text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
            V1 &mdash; Foundation
          </h2>
          <span class="text-sm font-medium px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-[var(--color-accent)] text-white">
            Live since May 2026
          </span>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-[var(--color-muted)]">
          Everything required to run a serious dog-walking business &mdash; multi-walker
          scheduling, intake, payments, reports &mdash; built around the dog rather than
          the invoice.
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-6 space-y-3 text-lg leading-relaxed">
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)] font-semibold">&#x2713;</span> The Window/Horizon scheduling model with a variable per-business commitment radius</li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)] font-semibold">&#x2713;</span> Self-onboarding QR card &rarr; structured intake &rarr; auto-Calendar Meet &amp; Greet</li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)] font-semibold">&#x2713;</span> Voice-to-tagged-events for walks (talk through the walk, get a structured timeline)</li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)] font-semibold">&#x2713;</span> Photos as durable dog memories with auto-generated hashtags</li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)] font-semibold">&#x2713;</span> The Poop Tracker: potty logging on the dog's record, building a rolling baseline for the vet conversation</li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)] font-semibold">&#x2713;</span> Tips that go to the walker</li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)] font-semibold">&#x2713;</span> Two-phase auto-positioning: regular-walker inference + statistical time prediction</li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)] font-semibold">&#x2713;</span> BYO Stripe Connect with billing cycles</li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)] font-semibold">&#x2713;</span> Multi-service architecture, proven by BarkVentures running in production at Hamilton Bark</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- V1.5 -->
      <section class="mt-20">
        <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between flex-wrap gap-2">
          <h2 class="font-display text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
            V1.5 &mdash; Self-Service
          </h2>
          <span class="text-sm font-medium px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-[var(--color-bg)] border border-[var(--color-rule)]">
            Anticipated Q3 2026
          </span>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-[var(--color-muted)]">
          Smoothing the walker-acquisition path so onboarding doesn't depend on a setup
          call, and turning on the AI assists that have been shipping in the background.
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-6 space-y-3 text-lg leading-relaxed">
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-[var(--color-muted)]">&middot;</span><span>Self-serve walker signup at sniffrpack.com &rarr; working tenant + Stripe Connect + admin login + branded subdomain end-to-end</span></li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-[var(--color-muted)]">&middot;</span><span>The free tier goes self-serve: Sniffr is <a href="/pricing" class="text-[var(--color-accent)] hover:underline">free until your fourth client pays</a></span></li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-[var(--color-muted)]">&middot;</span><span>AI-assist generate: auto-caption drafts on photos, auto-report drafts on walks (always editable; the walker stays in the driver's seat)</span></li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-[var(--color-muted)]">&middot;</span><span>Persisted per-dog personality summaries powering the AI assists</span></li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-[var(--color-muted)]">&middot;</span><span>Data import from Time To Pet, Scout, and Precise &mdash; making the switch a one-click, not a weekend</span></li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- V2 -->
      <section class="mt-20">
        <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between flex-wrap gap-2">
          <h2 class="font-display text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
            V2 &mdash; Network
          </h2>
          <span class="text-sm font-medium px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-[var(--color-bg)] border border-[var(--color-rule)]">
            Anticipated Q3 2026
          </span>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-[var(--color-muted)]">
          Walkers stop feeling like solo operators. The community starts to act like a
          labor network &mdash; covering each other's days off, sharing trust, getting
          paid for it cleanly.
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-6 space-y-3 text-lg leading-relaxed">
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-[var(--color-muted)]">&middot;</span><span>Tenant-to-tenant work sharing: hand a Window to another Sniffr walker at their rates</span></li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-[var(--color-muted)]">&middot;</span><span>Optional client-side M&amp;G workflow before a handoff (some clients say <em>"I trust anyone you trust"</em>; some don't &mdash; the system supports both)</span></li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-[var(--color-muted)]">&middot;</span><span>Tenant-to-tenant payout flow via Stripe Connect</span></li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-[var(--color-muted)]">&middot;</span><span>Each walker's coverage circle: the trusted nearby Sniffr walkers they can hand work to</span></li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-relaxed italic text-[var(--color-muted)]">
          V2 is when Sniffr stops being software for <em>one</em> walker's business and
          starts being connective tissue <em>between</em> businesses.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- V3 -->
      <section class="mt-20">
        <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between flex-wrap gap-2">
          <h2 class="font-display text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
            V3 &mdash; The Dog's Record
          </h2>
          <span class="text-sm font-medium px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-[var(--color-bg)] border border-[var(--color-rule)]">
            Anticipated Q4 2026
          </span>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-[var(--color-muted)]">
          Sniffr opens to dog families with no walker attached. The record stops being
          something you get because you hired someone, and becomes something your dog
          simply has.
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-6 space-y-3 text-lg leading-relaxed">
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-[var(--color-muted)]">&middot;</span><span>Tenant-free signup: download Sniffr, add your dog. No business required.</span></li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-[var(--color-muted)]">&middot;</span><span><strong>Story</strong>: photos, health, and daily life in one timeline. When you do have a walker, their reports land in the same stream you write in.</span></li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-[var(--color-muted)]">&middot;</span><span>The Poop Tracker's rolling baseline becomes the promise: the log your vet wishes you had, and the one thing you can't build retroactively</span></li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-[var(--color-muted)]">&middot;</span><span>Photo import that shows you the output first: let Sniffr find your dog in the last 30 days of your camera roll, and see the month as a captioned story before you decide to go further back</span></li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-[var(--color-muted)]">&middot;</span><span><strong>Share with vet</strong>: a date-ranged PDF of the whole record &mdash; poop baseline, dated photos, service history across every provider. No single business can produce it. The owner can.</span></li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-[var(--color-muted)]">&middot;</span><span>Connect the assistant your family already uses &mdash; Claude, ChatGPT, or Gemini &mdash; and ask <em>"how was Wally's week?"</em> against the real record. <span class="text-[var(--color-muted)]">(Connector built; shipping pending security hardening so a client agent can't bypass tenant rules.)</span></span></li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-relaxed italic text-[var(--color-muted)]">
          One record, many authors, the owner holds it. When a walker joins later, they
          don't hand you a portal into their system &mdash; they fill the gaps in a record
          you already own.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- V4 -->
      <section class="mt-20">
        <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between flex-wrap gap-2">
          <h2 class="font-display text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
            V4 &mdash; Community
          </h2>
          <span class="text-sm font-medium px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-[var(--color-bg)] border border-[var(--color-rule)]">
            Anticipated Q4 2026 / Early 2027
          </span>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-[var(--color-muted)]">
          The social graph the record has been quietly computing surfaces as Circles and
          Packs. This is why the record opens to families first: dogs accumulate at the
          same parks, and the community features need that density, not a sales team.
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-6 space-y-3 text-lg leading-relaxed">
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-[var(--color-muted)]">&middot;</span><span><strong>Circles</strong> &mdash; your dog's auto-detected network of dogs they've actually met. Triggered when a recognized friend's owner is at the same park at the same time. Confirmed by the photo uploader. No facial-recognition ML &mdash; geofence + app metadata + a one-tap <em>"is that Goldie?"</em> prompt gets us there.</span></li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-[var(--color-muted)]">&middot;</span><span>Photos of your dog that you didn't take: when a Circle photo is confirmed, both families receive it</span></li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-[var(--color-muted)]">&middot;</span><span><strong>Packs</strong> &mdash; branded human communities that form around shared parks and times. Invite links, shared photo streams, event management, and a Pack fund.</span></li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-[var(--color-muted)]">&middot;</span><span>Walker advertising against Packs: <em>"20% of June's walks booked through this link goes to the Sunday Morning Dachshund Pack."</em></span></li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-[var(--color-muted)]">&middot;</span><span>The referral network made visible, measurable, and economically active.</span></li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-relaxed italic text-[var(--color-muted)]">
          V4 is when the consumer side of Sniffr starts driving walker acquisition on its
          own. Owners love their Pack, push their walker to join Sniffr. Walkers join
          because their Pack is here. The flywheel closes.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- V5 -->
      <section class="mt-20">
        <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between flex-wrap gap-2">
          <h2 class="font-display text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
            V5 &mdash; Every Service
          </h2>
          <span class="text-sm font-medium px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-[var(--color-bg)] border border-[var(--color-rule)]">
            Anticipated 2027
          </span>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-[var(--color-muted)]">
          Boarding, daycare, grooming, and training &mdash; each one a new author on the
          same record, and a new kind of business Sniffr serves.
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-6 space-y-3 text-lg leading-relaxed">
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-[var(--color-muted)]">&middot;</span><span>Service plugins on the architecture BarkVentures already proves in production</span></li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-[var(--color-muted)]">&middot;</span><span>Each service deepens the dog's record and opens a new market at once: the groomer is a different business, the dog is the same dog. Their grooming records carry their brand; your walk reports carry yours; the family sees one timeline.</span></li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-[var(--color-muted)]">&middot;</span><span><strong>Bespoke service shapes</strong>: Hamilton Bark designed BarkVenture for mountain trips with their dogs; if you have a service shape that doesn't exist yet, talk to us. Once we build it, every Sniffr business can use it.</span></li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- How we ship -->
      <section class="mt-24 pt-16 border-t border-[var(--color-rule)]">
        <h2 class="font-display text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
          How we ship
        </h2>

        <div class="mt-8 space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed">
          <p>
            Most software in this space comes from one of two places. <strong>Marketplaces</strong>
            like Rover and Wag &mdash; VC-backed, take a cut from both sides of every
            transaction, and treat your customers as inventory. Or <strong>invoicing
            platforms</strong> like Time To Pet, Scout, and Precise &mdash; older, slower,
            originally built around the bill and retrofitted with everything else over the
            years. Both scope the dog's history to the business that made it. Sniffr scopes
            it to the dog.
          </p>
          <p>
            Sniffr is neither. It's a product of <strong>Papyrus Labs AI</strong>, a research
            lab working at the intersection of AI and human cognition. <span class="text-[var(--color-muted)]"><em>(Other Papyrus Labs products include Seshat, structural code intelligence used by AI agents.)</em></span> Sniffr is the lab's applied
            dog-care project &mdash; and the only one with a working dog-walking business
            shipping every line of code in production.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Hamilton Bark runs ~130 walks a week, $250K/year in service revenue,
            on Sniffr today.</strong> Every feature listed above survives contact with
            that business or it doesn't ship.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Your Stripe is your Stripe. Your customers are yours.</strong> Sniffr
            is software, not a marketplace. We don't broker your relationships, take a
            cut of your customer revenue, or hold your book of business hostage. When you
            leave us, your customers leave with you. That's not a feature &mdash; it's the
            whole stance, and it's the reason Sniffr exists.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Built fast, by one founder, without outside funding.</strong> Sniffr's
            velocity comes from Papyrus Labs' custom multi-agent build infrastructure
            &mdash; the same class of tooling that lets a small team out-ship a venture-backed
            eight. That's how a single founder ships an entire year of features in a year,
            against a real production customer, without taking money that would force the
            product to extract from the people using it.
          </p>
          <p class="italic text-[var(--color-muted)]">
            Anticipated dates are anticipated, not promised &mdash; but the tables are
            built, the plugins are partially written, and the agents are running. We'll
            move dates as we learn, but not by years.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-12">
          <a
            href="/#book"
            class="bg-[var(--color-ink)] text-[var(--color-bg)] px-6 py-3 rounded-md font-medium hover:bg-[var(--color-accent)] transition-colors inline-block"
          >
            Book a setup call
          </a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
